src folder is the starting point for a GUI creation with QtDesigner and PySide6

open the python folder in vs code. Install 'Qt for Python' pluging in VS Code

Then when you have openend the python folder, right click the designer/main_window.ui file and press 'Compile Qt Ui File'. You have to do that once in the beginning. From now on, it will always auto generate the main_window_ui.py file out of the .ui file. Make sure to choose a python version that has the necessary modules installed (PySide6). 

the src folder structe was generated by the fbs software. Its a paid software you can buy here: https://build-system.fman.io/
It is not needed for creating the GUI and running it on linux. Probably also not for generating a .exe. But it is probably worth buing it because packaging, licensing and so on is all done by that fbs module. If you want to use it commericially in the future.

For now, for developing, it is not needed. (in main.py: fbs = False)
